#: src/languages/php.md:152
msgid "These are common troubleshooting tips, in case you run into issues:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:154
msgid ""
"Ensure that you have Xdebug installed for the version of PHP you're running."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:155
msgid "Ensure that Xdebug is configured to run in `debug` mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:156
msgid "Ensure that Xdebug is actually starting a debugging session."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:157
msgid "Ensure that the host and port matches between Xdebug and Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:158
msgid ""
"Look at the diagnostics log by using the `xdebug_info()` function in the "
"page you're trying to debug."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:160
msgid "Using the Tailwind CSS Language Server with PHP"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:162
msgid ""
"To get all the features (autocomplete, linting, etc.) from the [Tailwind CSS "
"language server](https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss-intellisense/"
"tree/HEAD/packages/tailwindcss-language-server#readme) in PHP files, you "
"need to configure the language server so that it knows about where to look "
"for CSS classes by adding the following to your `settings.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:167 src/languages/php.md:203
msgid "\"tailwindcss-language-server\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:168 src/languages/php.md:204
msgid "\"settings\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:169 src/languages/php.md:205
msgid "\"includeLanguages\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:170 src/languages/php.md:206
msgid "\"php\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:170 src/languages/php.md:206 src/languages/php.md:207
msgid "\"html\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:172 src/languages/php.md:209
msgid "\"experimental\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:173 src/languages/php.md:210
msgid "\"classRegex\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:174 src/languages/php.md:211
msgid "\"class=\\\"([^\\\"]*)\\\"\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:175 src/languages/php.md:212
msgid "\"class='([^']*)'\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:176 src/languages/php.md:213
msgid "\"class=\\\\\\\"([^\\\\\\\"]*)\\\\\\\"\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:185
msgid ""
"With these settings, you will get completions for Tailwind CSS classes in "
"HTML attributes inside PHP files. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:188
msgid "// PHP file with HTML:\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:191
msgid "\"flex items-center <completion here>\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:192
msgid "\"text-lg font-bold <completion here>\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:196
msgid "Laravel/Blade"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:198
msgid ""
"For Laravel/Blade files, you may need additional configuration to handle "
"Blade directives:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:207
msgid "\"blade\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:214
msgid "\"@class\\\\(\\\\[([^\\\\]]*)\\\\]\\\\)\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:223
msgid "This will also provide completions in Blade directives like:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/php.md:225
msgid ""
"```blade\n"
"{{-- Blade file --}}\n"
"<div class=\"flex {{ $customClass }} <completion here>\">\n"
"  @class(['flex', 'items-center', '<completion here>'])\n"
"</div>\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
